            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "<p>We’re delighted to be back at the wonderful Eastway Baths in Hackney Wick, for our Autumn 2026 edition of MicroActs - we'll be showcasing this fantastic collection of films in The Hall of this community hub in East London!</p><p>Join us on Thursday 24th September at 7pm for an evening of experimental short films, each 6mins or less, from an international &amp; UK based lineup of filmmakers. This programme features films from 5 continents, including Brazil, China, Colombia, France, Greece, Hong Kong, Italy, Republic of Korea, Mexico, New Zealand, Singapore, Tunisia, UK, Ukraine &amp; USA. Whether you’re a film lover or filmmaker, a creative, or simply curious, MicroActs is a film night not to be missed!</p><p>MicroActs creates low-cost &amp; accessible film events that showcase independent artists/filmmakers from around the world and champions the weird and wonderful. Discover the extraordinary genre of Artist Film in a welcoming space and connect with the MicroActs community. You can expect an evening of short films that defy genre and create conversations; exploring diverse themes such as cultural heritage, personal experience, queer identity, political activism &amp; the absurd. We look forward to seeing you at our third edition of the year and sharing a thought-provoking programme of shorts.</p><p><em><em>Please note, our screenings contain mature themes, and are recommended 16+. Please be advised that some of the films in this edition feature flashing imagery, thank you.</em></em></p>",
              "alignment": "left",
              "url": null,
              "alt": null,
              "caption": null,
              "imageId": null,
              "originalUrl": null,
              "width": null,
              "height": null,
              "embedUrl": null
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "<p><strong><strong>Curated by Liberty Antonia Sadler &amp; Jhenelle White</strong></strong></p><p>Check out <a href=\"http://microactslondon.com\" title=\"http://microactslondon.com\" target=\"_blank\" data-msys-clicktrack=\"0\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">microactslondon.com</a> to see our Filmmaker Archive, featuring all of the artists &amp; filmmakers we've showcased in our events.</p><p><strong><strong>7pm Doors</strong></strong></p><p><strong><strong>7.30pm Artist Film Programme Begins</strong></strong></p><p><strong><strong>Open till 10pm</strong></strong></p><p><em><em>Our Short Film Programme will be presented in 2 parts of approximately 40 minutes in each section, there will be a 20 min interval between halves.</em></em></p><p>To keep our accessible screenings going, we’ll be moving to a donation ticket model to help support these nights. We are proud to be a low cost event, all donations go back into keeping these screenings running and keeping them open to all, donations can be as low as £1 and any donation is greatly appreciated. If this is a barrier for you, please get in touch with us <a href=\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/o/microacts-17916239886?aff=ebdsshcopyurl\" title=\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/o/microacts-17916239886?aff=ebdsshcopyurl\" target=\"_blank\" data-msys-clicktrack=\"0\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">here</a> - many thanks!</p>",
